[model] lru_ttl_cache.py
[model] 
[model] A comprehensive, thread-safe, LRU (Least Recently Used) cache implementation
[model] with Time-To-Live (TTL) expiry support. This module provides a high-performance
[model] caching mechanism suitable for concurrent applications, offering both memory
[model] efficiency and data freshness guarantees.
[model] 
[model] Key Features:
[model] - LRU eviction policy when capacity is exceeded.
[model] - TTL-based automatic expiration of entries.
[model] - Thread-safe operations using internal locks and atomic operations.
[model] - Support for custom key generators and value serializers.
[model] - Configuration via class parameters or instance attributes.
[model] - Extensive test suite using pytest to validate correctness, performance,
[model]   and edge cases.
[model] 
[model] Usage Example:
[model]     from lru_ttl_cache import LRUTTLCache
[model] 
[model]     cache = LRUTTLCache(max_size=100, default_ttl=3600)
[model]     cache.set('user:1', {'name': 'Alice'}, ttl=10)
[model]     value = cache.get('user:1')
[model]     # value is {'name': 'Alice'}
[model]     # After 10 seconds, the entry expires.
[model]     # cache.get('user:1') returns None.
[model] 
[model]     # Eviction example:
